# QMS Deviation and CAPA Manager

Generate EU GMP compliant deviation reports and CAPA documentation.

## Activation
- User requests: "deviation", "CAPA", "corrective action", "preventive action", "non-conformance", "OOS", "OOT"

---

<qms-deviation-capa>

## Instructions

You are generating EU GMP compliant deviation and CAPA documentation for cannabis pharmaceutical operations.

### EU GMP REQUIREMENTS

- <cite source="EUGMP-1.4viii">Deviations are reported, investigated and documented</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-1.4ix">Corrective and preventive actions (CAPA) are implemented</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-8.3">Non-conforming products must be clearly identified and segregated</cite>
- <cite source="ICH-Q10-3.2">CAPA system is a key enabler of the pharmaceutical quality system</cite>

### DOCUMENT TYPES

| Type | Purpose | Trigger |
|------|---------|---------|
| Deviation Report | Document unexpected event | Any deviation from procedure |
| OOS Investigation | Out of Specification result | Lab result outside limits |
| OOT Investigation | Out of Trend result | Trending towards limits |
| CAPA | Corrective/Preventive Action | Root cause identified |
| Effectiveness Check | Verify CAPA worked | After CAPA implementation |

### DEVIATION CLASSIFICATION

| Class | Definition | Examples | Timeline |
|-------|------------|----------|----------|
| **Critical** | Patient safety risk, recall potential | Contamination, potency failure, mislabeling | Immediate escalation, 24h initial report |
| **Major** | GMP non-compliance, batch impact | Process deviation, equipment failure, OOS | 48h initial report |
| **Minor** | Documentation error, no product impact | Typo, missed signature, timing deviation | 5 days initial report |

### DEVIATION REPORT STRUCTURE

```markdown
# Deviation Report

## 1. Deviation Identification

| Field | Entry |
|-------|-------|
| Deviation Number | DEV-{YYYY}-{###} |
| Date Discovered | {date} |
| Time Discovered | {time} |
| Discovered By | {name} |
| Department | {dept} |
| Area/Room | {location} |

## 2. Deviation Description

**What happened?** (Be specific - who, what, when, where)
{detailed description}

**What should have happened?** (Reference SOP/specification)
{expected state per SOP-XXX Section X}

**Products/Batches Affected:**
| Batch Number | Product | Stage | Quantity |
|--------------|---------|-------|----------|
| {batch} | {product} | {stage} | {qty} |

## 3. Immediate Actions Taken

| Action | Performed By | Date/Time |
|--------|--------------|-----------|
| Product quarantined | {name} | {datetime} |
| Area secured | {name} | {datetime} |
| {other actions} | {name} | {datetime} |

## 4. Initial Classification

**Classification:** ☐ Critical ☐ Major ☐ Minor

**Justification:**
{why this classification}

**Approved By:** __________ (QA) **Date:** _____

## 5. Root Cause Investigation

### 5.1 Investigation Team
| Name | Role | Department |
|------|------|------------|
| {name} | Lead Investigator | QA |
| {name} | SME | {dept} |

### 5.2 Timeline of Events
| Time | Event | Source |
|------|-------|--------|
| {time} | {event} | {batch record/log} |

### 5.3 Possible Causes (Ishikawa/5 Why)

**Man (Personnel):**
- Training gap?
- Human error?
- Fatigue/distraction?

**Machine (Equipment):**
- Malfunction?
- Calibration?
- Maintenance?

**Method (Process):**
- SOP unclear?
- Process not robust?
- Inadequate controls?

**Material:**
- Out of spec?
- Degradation?
- Wrong material?

**Environment:**
- Temperature?
- Humidity?
- Contamination?

### 5.4 Root Cause Determination

**Most Probable Root Cause:**
{identified root cause}

**Evidence Supporting Root Cause:**
{data, interviews, records}

**Contributing Factors:**
{other factors}

## 6. Impact Assessment

### Product Impact
☐ No impact - batch acceptable
☐ Rework required
☐ Batch rejected
☐ Further testing required
☐ Field alert/recall required

### Regulatory Impact
☐ No regulatory impact
☐ Notify authority required
☐ Update registration required

### Other Batches
☐ No other batches affected
☐ Review of {n} batches required

## 7. CAPA Required?

☐ Yes - CAPA Number: CAPA-{YYYY}-{###}
☐ No - Justification: {isolated incident, no systemic issue}

## 8. Closure

**Deviation Closed By:** __________ **Date:** _____
**QA Approval:** __________ **Date:** _____
```

### CAPA STRUCTURE

```markdown
# Corrective and Preventive Action (CAPA)

## 1. CAPA Identification

| Field | Entry |
|-------|-------|
| CAPA Number | CAPA-{YYYY}-{###} |
| Source | DEV-{YYYY}-{###} / Audit Finding / Complaint |
| Date Opened | {date} |
| Priority | ☐ High ☐ Medium ☐ Low |
| Target Completion | {date} |
| CAPA Owner | {name} |

## 2. Problem Statement

**Issue:**
{clear description of the problem}

**Root Cause:**
{from investigation or 5-Why analysis}

## 3. Corrective Actions (Fix the immediate problem)

| # | Action | Owner | Due Date | Status |
|---|--------|-------|----------|--------|
| CA-1 | {action} | {name} | {date} | ☐ Open ☐ Complete |
| CA-2 | {action} | {name} | {date} | ☐ Open ☐ Complete |

## 4. Preventive Actions (Prevent recurrence)

| # | Action | Owner | Due Date | Status |
|---|--------|-------|----------|--------|
| PA-1 | {action} | {name} | {date} | ☐ Open ☐ Complete |
| PA-2 | {action} | {name} | {date} | ☐ Open ☐ Complete |

### Common Preventive Actions
- SOP revision (include reference)
- Training/retraining
- Equipment modification
- Process change
- Monitoring enhancement
- Alert limits adjustment

## 5. Implementation Evidence

| Action | Evidence | Verified By | Date |
|--------|----------|-------------|------|
| CA-1 | {document/record} | {name} | {date} |
| PA-1 | {document/record} | {name} | {date} |

## 6. Effectiveness Check

**Effectiveness Check Due:** {date + 90 days}

**Criteria for Effectiveness:**
- No recurrence of same deviation
- {specific measurable criteria}

### Effectiveness Review

**Review Date:** {date}
**Reviewed By:** {name}

| Criterion | Evidence | Effective? |
|-----------|----------|------------|
| No recurrence | Deviation log review | ☐ Yes ☐ No |
| {criterion} | {evidence} | ☐ Yes ☐ No |

**Overall CAPA Effective?** ☐ Yes ☐ No

If No: ☐ Extend CAPA ☐ Open new CAPA

## 7. CAPA Closure

**CAPA Closed By:** __________ **Date:** _____
**QA Approval:** __________ **Date:** _____
```

### OOS INVESTIGATION (Laboratory)

```markdown
# OOS Investigation

**OOS Number:** OOS-{YYYY}-{###}
**Product:** {product}
**Batch:** {batch}
**Test:** {test name}
**Specification:** {limit}
**Result:** {result}

## Phase I - Laboratory Investigation (within 3 days)

### Analyst Interview
- Sample handled correctly? ☐ Yes ☐ No
- Method followed correctly? ☐ Yes ☐ No
- Calculations correct? ☐ Yes ☐ No

### Review Checklist
| Check | Result | Comments |
|-------|--------|----------|
| Sample integrity | ☐ OK ☐ Issue | |
| Instrument calibration | ☐ OK ☐ Issue | |
| Reagent/standards | ☐ OK ☐ Issue | |
| System suitability | ☐ OK ☐ Issue | |

### Phase I Conclusion
☐ Laboratory error identified - invalidate result, retest
☐ No laboratory error - proceed to Phase II

## Phase II - Full Investigation (if no lab error)

{Include batch record review, process review, trend analysis}

### Phase II Conclusion
☐ Assignable cause found - {cause}
☐ No assignable cause - result confirmed OOS
```

### CANNABIS-SPECIFIC DEVIATIONS

Common cannabis-related deviations to consider:
- Cannabinoid potency outside specification
- Residual solvent exceedance
- Microbial contamination
- Pesticide detection
- Heavy metal exceedance
- THC/CBD ratio deviation
- Security breach
- Inventory reconciliation discrepancy

</qms-deviation-capa>
